<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saverne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zabern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saverne (German Zabern) is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, where the road from Strasbourg crosses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. After 1262 it was the main residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Strasbourg, whose great Château des Rohan was rebuilt there from 1779. In May 1525 Duke Antoine of Lorraine destroyed a peasant army near the town during the German Peasants' War, and in 1913 incidents with the German garrison caused the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saverne-affair">Zabern Affair</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saverne.jpg" alt="Saverne" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rolf Krahl (Rotkraut) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chateau_Rohan_Saverne_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1525 Duke Antoine destroyed a peasant army of the German Peasants’ War near <b>Saverne</b> in Alsace.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Strasbourg became in effect a self-governing free imperial city, and the bishops moved their seat to <b>Saverne</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-8">8 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1262 the citizens defeated Bishop Walter of Geroldseck at Hausbergen and the city became the Free Imperial City of Strasbourg, so the bishops governed from <b>Saverne</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-strasbourg">Prince-Bishopric of Strasbourg</a></li></ul></section>
